% Problematic hypoglycemia without insulin: Hal with three level 2 events
% after two medication adjustments (claim 1); Ida with one level 3 event
% that needed third party assistance (claim 2); Jo with one level 2 event
% only (claim 3).
scenario cgm_problematic_hypoglycemia is:
    claim 1 is for the CGM of Hal.
    the HCPCS code of the CGM of Hal is "E2103".
    the CGM of Hal is furnished to Hal.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the diagnosis code of Hal is "E11.65".
    the finding trained on continuous glucose monitor about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the CGM of Hal is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    3 level two hypoglycemic events are documented for Hal.
    2 medication adjustments before the most recent level two event are documented for Hal.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Hal to evaluate diabetes control on 2026-01-10.
    the order for the CGM of Hal is dated 2026-02-20.
    claim 2 is for the CGM of Ida.
    the HCPCS code of the CGM of Ida is "E2103".
    the CGM of Ida is furnished to Ida.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-03-01.
    the diagnosis code of Ida is "E11.9".
    the finding trained on continuous glucose monitor about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the CGM of Ida is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    1 level three hypoglycemic events are documented for Ida.
    third party assistance for treatment of hypoglycemia is documented for Ida.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Ida to evaluate diabetes control on 2026-01-10.
    the order for the CGM of Ida is dated 2026-02-20.
    claim 3 is for the CGM of Jo.
    the HCPCS code of the CGM of Jo is "E2103".
    the CGM of Jo is furnished to Jo.
    the date of service of claim 3 is 2026-03-01.
    the diagnosis code of Jo is "E11.9".
    the finding trained on continuous glucose monitor about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the CGM of Jo is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    1 level two hypoglycemic events are documented for Jo.
    2 medication adjustments before the most recent level two event are documented for Jo.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Jo to evaluate diabetes control on 2026-01-10.
    the order for the CGM of Jo is dated 2026-02-20.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The CGM supply allowance (A4239) nine months after the initial
% prescription, 3 units for 90 days: the visit documenting adherence
% eleven weeks before the date of service supports continued coverage.
scenario cgm_supply_continued_with_visit is:
    claim 1 is for the supply allowance.
    the HCPCS code of the supply allowance is "A4239".
    the supply allowance is an accessory of the CGM.
    the supply allowance is furnished to Fay.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 3.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the HCPCS code of the CGM is "E2103".
    the CGM is furnished to Fay.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "E10.9".
    the finding trained on continuous glucose monitor about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the CGM is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    Fay is currently being treated with insulin.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Fay to evaluate diabetes control on 2025-05-10.
    the order for the CGM is dated 2025-06-01.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Fay to document adherence to the CGM regimen on 2025-12-10.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

