% A refill of lancets (A4259, 1 unit of 100 for three months) for Ann: the
% beneficiary's affirmation 16 days before the supply runs out, delivery 4
% days before, the continued-need record, the order — payable.
scenario lancets_refill is:
    claim 1 is for the lancets.
    the HCPCS code of the lancets is "A4259".
    the lancets is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 1.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "E11.9".
    the finding trained on blood glucose monitor about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the current supply of the lancets is expected to end on 2026-06-05.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the lancets on 2026-05-20.
    the medical record documents continued need for the lancets on 2026-02-20.
    the record documents continued use of the lancets on 2026-05-20.
    the order for the lancets is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the lancets is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the lancets includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the lancets includes order date.
    the order for the lancets includes description of the item.
    the order for the lancets includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the lancets includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the lancets was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the lancets was delivered on 2026-06-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the lancets.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

